      {
       "id": "69f880d4bbf1d3145596842b",
       "headline": "Qualcomm reported quarterly earnings on Wednesday that beat Wall Street estimates and announced a major sale of AI chips, prompting its stock to jump nearly 17% in after-hours trading. The San Diego-based wireless pioneer earned $7.370 billion, or $6.88 per share, on revenue of $10.599 billion in the second fiscal quarter ended March 29, compared to $2.812 billion, or $2.52 per share, on revenue of $10.979 billion in the same quarter a year ago.",
